  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Mobilization Initiative to End Tuberculosis (COMMIT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  The Community Mobilization Initiative to End Tuberculosis (COMMIT) collaborates with the National Tuberculosis (TB) Program (NTP) to increase TB case detection, improve the quality of treatment, and prevent disease transmission in 14 established districts. COMMIT works with the NTP and the World Health Organization on development and implementation of the multi-sectoral accountability framework, which includes the private sector. COMMIT delivers technical assistance to the NTP for introduction and scale-up of diagnostic connectivity and improved links with the TB Management Information System (TB-MIS) and expansion of TB-MIS down to the health center level. ..USAID awarded COMMIT through a competitive process in which the offeror with the best value to the U.S. government was selected, in accordance with federal procurement regulations. Further, the implementing partner has extensive TB detection experience in the 14 districts where it works...The activity falls under the administration&apos;s priority to assert U.S. leadership in &quot;Advancing global health security, and mitigating development and humanitarian impacts&quot; by supporting the Agency&apos;s inclusive development strategy in expanding the access to key risk populations in the remote and underserved supported districts. In addition, the activity contributes to USAID/Cambodia&apos;s CDCS 2020-2025 Development Objective 2 &quot;To improve quality of and access to priority health services in Cambodia&quot; and the ICS Mission Objective 2.3, Sub-objective 2.3.1, &quot;By 2024, quality of and access to priority health services improved.&quot;..</narrative>
  </description>
